1
00:00:01,083 --> 00:00:03,250
No one betrays me!

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,750
I'd say we just proved
that's not true.

3
00:00:05,833 --> 00:00:07,125
Nokt?

4
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:08,792
-[whooshes]
-[Ras] Ah!

5
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:11,583
[growls]

6
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:14,583
[Sora, Lloyd grunt]

7
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:16,250
Yah! [grunts]

8
00:00:25,542 --> 00:00:27,083
[gunfire]

9
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:28,625
[straining]

10
00:00:30,333 --> 00:00:32,042
[grunts]

11
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:34,500
-Yah!
-[clangs]

12
00:00:34,583 --> 00:00:36,458
-[gunfire]
-[clangs]

13
00:00:36,542 --> 00:00:37,708
[grunts]

14
00:00:37,792 --> 00:00:39,417
Let me tell you something,

15
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,167
going from having
half the Elemental Powers

16
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,333
in the Tournament
to absolutely none? [grunts]

17
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:45,708
-Not ideal.
-[both grunt]

18
00:00:45,792 --> 00:00:49,083
Arin told me the dragon horns
are at that strange Monastery.

19
00:00:49,167 --> 00:00:51,167
[grunts] I would have
bet everything

20
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:53,375
Ras was behind this.
I was so wrong.

21
00:00:53,458 --> 00:00:55,625
[both grunting]

22
00:00:55,708 --> 00:00:57,542
Don't be so hard on yourself.

23
00:00:57,625 --> 00:01:00,375
Jordana being taken over
by an ancient evil soul

24
00:01:00,458 --> 00:01:02,958
was not something anyone
factored into the equation.

25
00:01:03,042 --> 00:01:05,708
We gotta keep Nokt and Rox
from getting to that Monastery

26
00:01:05,792 --> 00:01:08,500
to free the rest
of the Forbidden Five!

27
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:10,458
It might be too late for that!

28
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:14,208
Get back here!

29
00:01:14,292 --> 00:01:16,958
Those Elemental Powers
belong to me!

30
00:01:17,042 --> 00:01:18,958
[roars]

31
00:01:19,042 --> 00:01:20,333
[grunts]

32
00:01:21,792 --> 00:01:24,000
[gunfire]

33
00:01:25,083 --> 00:01:26,833
[grunting]

34
00:01:32,792 --> 00:01:34,417
I knew Lloyd wouldn't listen

35
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,250
when I told him Master Wu
caused the Merge.

36
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:37,917
I just knew it!

37
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,750
Arin, that information
is a lot to process.

38
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:42,333
What's to process?

39
00:01:42,417 --> 00:01:44,333
Your teacher disrupted
all the realms!

40
00:01:44,417 --> 00:01:47,292
He caused
my parents to disappear!

41
00:01:47,375 --> 00:01:50,083
[Cole grunting]

42
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:52,667
Ugh! These things
are welded on tight!

43
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:54,375
The games are almost over,
Cole.

44
00:01:54,458 --> 00:01:56,458
And if Ras wins,
he'll be here in a split second

45
00:01:56,542 --> 00:01:58,917
to use these horns to get
to the Source Dragons.

46
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,500
-We gotta hurry!
-[crash]

47
00:02:00,583 --> 00:02:02,167
-Did you hear that?
-[crash]

48
00:02:02,250 --> 00:02:03,917
[crash]

49
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Be prepared for anything.
[grunts]

50
00:02:08,125 --> 00:02:10,542
-[Riyu warbles]
-Nya!

51
00:02:10,625 --> 00:02:13,750
-[laughs]
-This is most unexpected.

52
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:17,375
Tell me about it.
Riyu and I found a way
to talk to Kai.

53
00:02:17,458 --> 00:02:18,875
Riyu gives me a spark,

54
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:20,625
and my connection
with my brother

55
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:22,458
lets me use some dragon ivory
to speak to him.

56
00:02:22,542 --> 00:02:24,583
Dragon ivory like
from those horns?

57
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:27,000
[Nya] Exactly! Apparently,
Dragon Crowns

58
00:02:27,083 --> 00:02:28,833
can communicate
with the Nether-Space,

59
00:02:28,917 --> 00:02:31,542
and could be our key
to freeing Kai and Bonzle.

60
00:02:31,625 --> 00:02:34,958
But unfortunately, could
also free the Forbidden Five.

61
00:02:35,042 --> 00:02:36,875
How did you determine
all of this?

62
00:02:36,958 --> 00:02:38,917
We overheard it when
we were being captured by--

63
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,125
[gasps] Them!

64
00:02:42,208 --> 00:02:44,458
♪ Lost in the unknown
So much to see ♪

65
00:02:44,542 --> 00:02:47,750
- ♪ Together we will rise! ♪
-♪ Yeah! ♪

66
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:50,875
♪ We fight ♪

67
00:02:50,958 --> 00:02:54,542
♪ Be a Ninja
For what's right! ♪

68
00:02:55,667 --> 00:02:57,375
[flames roaring]

69
00:02:59,917 --> 00:03:02,042
[Cole]
Ninja, go!

70
00:03:03,833 --> 00:03:05,542
Yah!

71
00:03:05,625 --> 00:03:07,042
[grunts]

72
00:03:07,958 --> 00:03:10,000
You're not getting
to the Source Dragons!

73
00:03:10,083 --> 00:03:12,208
Ras's plans end now!

74
00:03:12,292 --> 00:03:15,292
Source Dragons? Ras?

75
00:03:15,375 --> 00:03:18,125
This has nothing
to do with them!

76
00:03:18,208 --> 00:03:20,333
This is all us.

77
00:03:20,417 --> 00:03:23,958
[laughs evilly]

78
00:03:26,458 --> 00:03:28,167
[grunts]

79
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:30,417
[growls]

80
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:34,333
This is not how I envisioned
our partnership ending,
Lord Ras.

81
00:03:34,417 --> 00:03:36,042
Partnership? Ha!

82
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:38,833
-But I thought we were friends!
-[grunts]

83
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:41,583
[grunts]

84
00:03:42,958 --> 00:03:45,000
Why you gotta
cramp my space?

85
00:03:45,083 --> 00:03:46,750
The Gamesmaster
is the only one

86
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:48,625
who can use the Element Cup.

87
00:03:48,708 --> 00:03:51,792
You alone have to drain Nokt
of the powers he stole.

88
00:03:51,875 --> 00:03:53,917
Mega agree,
but don't think this means

89
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,667
I forgot you tried
to hijack my games.

90
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:58,333
Uncool, Ras. Way uncool!

91
00:03:58,417 --> 00:04:00,958
No! Ras has Roby!

92
00:04:01,042 --> 00:04:03,000
They're probably
heading to Nokt,

93
00:04:03,083 --> 00:04:05,250
which is what
we should be doing!

94
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:07,000
[sighs] But we're needed here!

95
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:11,625
[Frak] Go after Nokt!
We can handle this!

96
00:04:11,708 --> 00:04:13,542
[grunts] I fought bullies

97
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:16,250
long before I became
Master of Quake. Hah!

98
00:04:16,333 --> 00:04:19,000
Yah! There's more to us
than elemental powers.

99
00:04:25,208 --> 00:04:26,417
You sure, Frak?

100
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,167
Ninja, go.

101
00:04:31,792 --> 00:04:34,667
You're just wasting our time!

102
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:36,042
[Rox yells]

103
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:40,667
[Rox, Nokt grunt]

104
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:43,583
Rising Dragon Technique
says otherwise.

105
00:04:43,667 --> 00:04:46,083
I sincerely detest
Rising Dragon.

106
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:49,833
Forget them. Go summon
the rest of the Five, brother.

107
00:04:49,917 --> 00:04:51,083
[grunts]

108
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:53,458
Brother?

109
00:04:55,042 --> 00:04:57,250
[attack yell]

110
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:58,958
Aah!

111
00:04:59,042 --> 00:05:00,000
[screeches]

112
00:05:00,083 --> 00:05:01,792
Aah!

113
00:05:06,042 --> 00:05:07,667
[screeches]

114
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,125
Shatterspin's not
the only fighting skill

115
00:05:10,208 --> 00:05:12,083
I can perform with this body--

116
00:05:12,167 --> 00:05:15,167
[groans]

117
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:19,083
Stop! I'm in control! Not you!

118
00:05:19,167 --> 00:05:21,417
[groaning]

119
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,917
[as Jordana]
Ninja, get out of here!

120
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,833
I don't know how long
I can stop Rox!

121
00:05:26,917 --> 00:05:28,208
What's happening to you?

122
00:05:28,292 --> 00:05:31,458
I can't hold her! Get away!

123
00:05:31,542 --> 00:05:33,042
[grunting]

124
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:34,292
[attack yell]

125
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,917
Ha!

126
00:05:37,708 --> 00:05:41,375
Frozen in place!
No one can defeat us!

127
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:44,792
[groans]

128
00:05:48,292 --> 00:05:51,250
At last, we will be free.

129
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:56,417
At last, all the merged realms
will fall beneath our might!

130
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,208
[rumbling]

131
00:05:59,333 --> 00:06:00,583
Surprise!

132
00:06:00,667 --> 00:06:02,000
[yells]

133
00:06:03,083 --> 00:06:04,792
[Nokt] Aah!

134
00:06:04,875 --> 00:06:08,292
Wow, true Spinjitzu
really is way more powerful.

135
00:06:08,375 --> 00:06:10,625
Do you really think
you have a chance at--

136
00:06:10,708 --> 00:06:13,583
Aah!

137
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,250
Next time, I drive.

138
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:18,958
[warbles]

139
00:06:19,042 --> 00:06:21,958
Frak taught you
my techniques well.

140
00:06:22,042 --> 00:06:25,667
You have achieved
proper Spinjitzu, Arin.

141
00:06:28,917 --> 00:06:31,208
Hopefully you knocked him out.
Be much easier to drain--

142
00:06:31,292 --> 00:06:32,750
Ah!

143
00:06:36,292 --> 00:06:38,000
Flank him!

144
00:06:38,083 --> 00:06:39,542
[grunts]

145
00:06:40,167 --> 00:06:41,208
[grunts]

146
00:06:41,292 --> 00:06:42,917
Roby! Now!

147
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,333
You've really crushed
my vibe, Nokt.

148
00:06:45,417 --> 00:06:47,917
Games are supposed
to be fun, dude.

149
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,375
Look it up.

150
00:06:50,375 --> 00:06:52,542
[roars]

151
00:06:53,875 --> 00:06:56,667
Aah!

152
00:06:59,125 --> 00:07:02,792
The Forbidden Five will enjoy
crushing you two first!

153
00:07:04,167 --> 00:07:06,167
[both scream, grunt]

154
00:07:06,250 --> 00:07:07,333
[groans]

155
00:07:08,958 --> 00:07:11,750
[rumbling]

156
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:14,125
Come to me, my brethren!

157
00:07:14,208 --> 00:07:17,667
You are finally free!

158
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:22,958
[explosions]

159
00:07:23,042 --> 00:07:26,917
[laughs] Master after master,

160
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,292
village after village,
army after army,

161
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:33,083
all crushed by the Five.

162
00:07:33,167 --> 00:07:36,000
Imagine the sheer
delusional ego needed

163
00:07:36,083 --> 00:07:37,542
to believe you could sto--

164
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:38,875
Ah!

165
00:07:38,958 --> 00:07:41,958
[groans]

166
00:07:42,042 --> 00:07:45,625
Okay, what was that?

167
00:07:45,708 --> 00:07:47,333
[zapping]

168
00:07:47,417 --> 00:07:49,083
[gasps]

169
00:07:50,333 --> 00:07:53,583
Rox! Good to see you, sister!

170
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:56,500
The real you.

171
00:07:57,333 --> 00:08:00,625
[groans] Ninja. While Rox
puppeted my body,

172
00:08:00,708 --> 00:08:03,000
I was trapped inside her mind.

173
00:08:03,083 --> 00:08:06,250
I've seen her thoughts,
her evil plans.

174
00:08:06,333 --> 00:08:08,083
You've got to stop her!

175
00:08:08,167 --> 00:08:10,417
Why aren't you doing anything?!

176
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:13,167
Would love to, but--

177
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:14,625
Oh! The static spell!

178
00:08:14,708 --> 00:08:17,083
-Ahh.
-Yes!

179
00:08:17,167 --> 00:08:19,667
Let's go. Can you
make a new bridge, Cole?

180
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:22,625
[grunts, groans]

181
00:08:22,708 --> 00:08:25,417
This mech doesn't have any
more Elemental energy in it!

182
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,125
We have to find
another way across.

183
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:28,500
[engine approaches]

184
00:08:31,167 --> 00:08:32,750
We can help with that!

185
00:08:35,875 --> 00:08:40,667
[grunting]

186
00:08:43,792 --> 00:08:46,417
[warbles]

187
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:49,458
[Ras groaning]

188
00:08:49,542 --> 00:08:51,042
[Arin grunts]

189
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:53,208
You would help me, Ninja?

190
00:08:53,292 --> 00:08:55,667
Look, we're not buddies
or anything,

191
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,500
but you know
where my parents are.

192
00:08:57,583 --> 00:08:59,750
I know a great many things,
Arin.

193
00:08:59,833 --> 00:09:02,083
I know the truth
about this universe.

194
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:04,792
-[strains]
-[thuds]

195
00:09:04,875 --> 00:09:06,667
I just want to find my parents.

196
00:09:12,375 --> 00:09:14,375
[Nokt] Did they
not survive the crossing?

197
00:09:14,458 --> 00:09:17,292
[Rox] They're alive. Just
drained by the corrupted method

198
00:09:17,375 --> 00:09:19,417
that we used to breech
the Nether-Space.

199
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:21,917
I too feel the strain.

200
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,042
We must get away,
somewhere to recover.

201
00:09:24,125 --> 00:09:26,875
[Lloyd] Sorry!
Vacation plans cancelled!

202
00:09:28,792 --> 00:09:30,792
You get your hands off my--

203
00:09:30,875 --> 00:09:32,667
Hey, where's Roby?

204
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,833
[Lloyd]
Ninja, go!

205
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,667
[grunts with effort]

206
00:09:43,417 --> 00:09:45,375
[grunting]

207
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:49,333
Yah!

208
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,458
All of you? Bah!

209
00:09:54,542 --> 00:09:56,917
I've never been more powerful!

210
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,250
Bring it on!

211
00:09:58,333 --> 00:10:00,208
[fighting grunts]

212
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:13,833
Aah!

213
00:10:15,417 --> 00:10:18,250
How did you learn
perfect Spinjitzu?

214
00:10:18,333 --> 00:10:19,708
Not from you.

215
00:10:21,625 --> 00:10:23,083
[Cole grunts]

216
00:10:27,917 --> 00:10:32,208
[whimpering] Ah!

217
00:10:32,292 --> 00:10:34,875
[gasping]

218
00:10:34,958 --> 00:10:37,208
Wyldfyre! Thank you!

219
00:10:37,292 --> 00:10:39,625
No prob.
It wasn't even a big deal

220
00:10:39,708 --> 00:10:41,458
because I didn't have
to overcome

221
00:10:41,542 --> 00:10:43,542
a crippling fear
of heights to do it.

222
00:10:43,625 --> 00:10:47,708
[grunts] I'll be the stang
to your zoot anytime.

223
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:50,333
[roars]

224
00:10:50,417 --> 00:10:51,500
What was that?

225
00:10:51,583 --> 00:10:52,958
A romance roar.

226
00:10:53,042 --> 00:10:55,042
In my culture,
the fire dragons,

227
00:10:55,125 --> 00:10:57,458
that's how we declare love.

228
00:10:58,292 --> 00:10:59,917
Roar!

229
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,875
Did... did I do that right?

230
00:11:01,958 --> 00:11:06,125
-[both roaring]
-[crash]

231
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:08,333
Come on! We gotta
get you and your Element Cup

232
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,667
back up there. Somehow.

233
00:11:10,750 --> 00:11:12,125
[intense music]

234
00:11:12,208 --> 00:11:14,917
[fighting grunts]

235
00:11:18,375 --> 00:11:19,542
[strains]

236
00:11:21,833 --> 00:11:23,125
Ah!

237
00:11:25,292 --> 00:11:27,208
[reverberates]

238
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:31,083
[crashing]

239
00:11:33,375 --> 00:11:34,625
[roars]

240
00:11:34,708 --> 00:11:36,833
[grunts]

241
00:11:36,917 --> 00:11:39,042
That's for thinking
the Forbidden Five

242
00:11:39,125 --> 00:11:41,542
would be pawns
in your game, Ras!

243
00:11:41,625 --> 00:11:43,750
We own the game!

244
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:45,583
[Arin]
No! Don't hurt him!

245
00:11:47,042 --> 00:11:48,417
Ah!

246
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:51,083
[grunting]

247
00:11:53,333 --> 00:11:55,917
[warbles]

248
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,958
-What, Riyu? What--
-[warbles]

249
00:11:58,042 --> 00:11:59,333
What about the horns?

250
00:11:59,417 --> 00:12:01,750
-[warbles]
-[gasps]

251
00:12:01,833 --> 00:12:04,958
Of course! My connection
through the dragon ivory!

252
00:12:07,208 --> 00:12:09,958
What are you doing?! Stop!

253
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:16,542
Don't you dare touch her!

254
00:12:16,625 --> 00:12:18,750
That's my sister!

255
00:12:18,833 --> 00:12:20,667
-[gasps]
-Kai!

256
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:22,000
Yeah!

257
00:12:24,042 --> 00:12:25,208
[cracks neck]

258
00:12:27,125 --> 00:12:28,708
[fighting grunts]

259
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,167
[reverberates]

260
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:34,167
Nah, I know that trick.

261
00:12:38,542 --> 00:12:41,583
I don't need Shatterspin
to stop you, Ninja!

262
00:12:43,667 --> 00:12:44,750
Yah!

263
00:12:47,958 --> 00:12:52,875
But I now have more Elemental
Powers than anyone in history!

264
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,875
Now, this is just annoying.

265
00:12:58,417 --> 00:13:00,250
[grunting]

266
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:01,667
Ah!

267
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:04,333
[grunts]

268
00:13:05,417 --> 00:13:06,583
[grunts]

269
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:09,000
[grunts]

270
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:10,375
I think I'll finish you

271
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:12,500
with your own student's
heat power.

272
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:15,500
A poetic end to the Red Ninja.

273
00:13:17,792 --> 00:13:18,958
Wha--

274
00:13:25,667 --> 00:13:27,833
No one ends the Red Ninja.

275
00:13:27,917 --> 00:13:31,292
Sorry, Nokt, had
to transfer your powers.

276
00:13:31,375 --> 00:13:33,750
It happens to all the losers.

277
00:13:34,667 --> 00:13:36,083
[Nokt gasps]

278
00:13:36,167 --> 00:13:38,708
In the name
of the Source Dragons,

279
00:13:38,792 --> 00:13:41,750
I honor the grand tradition
of the games

280
00:13:41,833 --> 00:13:44,250
by returning
all Elemental Powers

281
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:46,333
to their rightful owners!

282
00:13:46,417 --> 00:13:47,750
[whooshing]

283
00:13:49,208 --> 00:13:50,708
[epic music]

284
00:13:52,417 --> 00:13:53,542
Woohoo!

285
00:14:09,125 --> 00:14:10,917
[screeching]

286
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:22,750
[gasps]

287
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:26,417
It cannot, will not,
end like this!

288
00:14:28,875 --> 00:14:31,583
[Rox]
Nokt! Come on!

289
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:37,000
[Ras]
You'll pay for your betrayal--

290
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:39,917
[Nokt]
No! You shall pay!

291
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,083
My revenge on you
is not yet complete!

292
00:14:43,167 --> 00:14:44,667
No! I need him!

293
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:46,708
Arin, no! Wait!

294
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:50,542
Arin, stop!

295
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:54,000
[explosion]

296
00:14:55,292 --> 00:14:58,542
Arin! Arin!

297
00:14:58,625 --> 00:15:00,500
[Lloyd]
They-- They all got away.

298
00:15:00,583 --> 00:15:02,292
And they've got Arin.

299
00:15:02,375 --> 00:15:04,833
Arin chose to go with them.

300
00:15:07,542 --> 00:15:10,917
So, I see nothing exciting
has been happening

301
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,333
since I've been gone.

302
00:15:12,417 --> 00:15:13,708
[Wyldfyre]
Aww!

303
00:15:13,792 --> 00:15:15,708
[groans, laughs]

304
00:15:15,792 --> 00:15:18,333
So good to have you back, bro.

305
00:15:22,708 --> 00:15:24,708
Bonzle, it's good to see you.

306
00:15:25,917 --> 00:15:28,375
But seriously,
perfect entrance, you two.

307
00:15:30,625 --> 00:15:31,958
[whooshes]

308
00:15:32,875 --> 00:15:34,458
Master Wu?

309
00:15:41,625 --> 00:15:44,708
Never in the history
of the Tournament of Sources

310
00:15:44,792 --> 00:15:47,542
have we seen
anything like this.

311
00:15:47,625 --> 00:15:51,625
Betrayal by one sworn
to protect the games--

312
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:56,708
but never before have we seen
such brave, noble competitors

313
00:15:56,792 --> 00:15:59,042
who defended
the honor of the games,

314
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,000
and the lives
of their colleagues.

315
00:16:01,083 --> 00:16:03,583
[audience cheering]

316
00:16:03,667 --> 00:16:06,083
And though a winner
was already declared,

317
00:16:06,167 --> 00:16:10,208
as Gamesmaster,
I officially void that victory.

318
00:16:10,292 --> 00:16:12,167
Told you my games
would be unprecedented!

319
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:15,292
[cheering]

320
00:16:15,375 --> 00:16:17,708
I now declare the true winner,

321
00:16:17,792 --> 00:16:21,458
the greatest Elemental Master
in all the Merged Lands:

322
00:16:21,542 --> 00:16:25,542
Sora: The Elemental Master
of Technology!

323
00:16:25,625 --> 00:16:29,083
[cheering]

324
00:16:31,917 --> 00:16:35,083
This really is an
extreme victory extravaganza!

325
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:43,250
Thank you, again.

326
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:45,208
We couldn't have done it
without you!

327
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,833
Has anyone seen Jordana?

328
00:16:50,917 --> 00:16:54,625
No, not since she
stopped Rox's static spell.

329
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:57,458
If she didn't try to break
through Rox's control

330
00:16:57,542 --> 00:16:59,042
and get me those clues,

331
00:16:59,125 --> 00:17:01,250
we wouldn't have
solved this mystery.

332
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:03,000
I wanted to thank her.

333
00:17:03,083 --> 00:17:04,917
I'm surprised she
doesn't want to talk

334
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,625
to the Greatest Elemental
Master in the Merged Lands.

335
00:17:08,708 --> 00:17:10,333
Remember when you
used to insist

336
00:17:10,417 --> 00:17:12,583
you didn't have
an Elemental Power?

337
00:17:12,667 --> 00:17:15,542
[chuckles] Feels like
a million years ago.

338
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:20,375
I know you had your doubts
about being our Master,

339
00:17:20,458 --> 00:17:22,833
but I couldn't have done this
without you, Lloyd.

340
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:25,083
You and Arin inspire me.

341
00:17:26,042 --> 00:17:28,458
He and I had a falling out
during the tournament.

342
00:17:28,542 --> 00:17:30,500
Since the Merge, I--

343
00:17:30,583 --> 00:17:32,750
I've never been
without my best friend.

344
00:17:33,958 --> 00:17:36,750
We'll find him. I promise.

345
00:17:40,167 --> 00:17:42,875
But what if he doesn't
want to be found?

346
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:50,625
So, uh, I was wondering,

347
00:17:50,708 --> 00:17:52,042
do you really have to go?

348
00:17:52,125 --> 00:17:55,250
Um, uh, as much
as I wanna stay,

349
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:58,250
and trust me,
I really want to stay,

350
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:00,833
all the other Ninja
are helpless without me.

351
00:18:00,917 --> 00:18:02,500
I have to go back.

352
00:18:05,792 --> 00:18:09,625
But we'll stay in touch?

353
00:18:09,708 --> 00:18:13,542
Absolutely. I'll never forget
our first roar.

354
00:18:13,625 --> 00:18:15,292
[roars]

355
00:18:16,458 --> 00:18:18,250
Roar!

356
00:18:18,333 --> 00:18:20,292
[both roaring]

357
00:18:20,375 --> 00:18:22,250
Uh, Wyldfyre?

358
00:18:22,333 --> 00:18:24,000
Time to go, cutie.

359
00:18:26,417 --> 00:18:28,125
How are we getting home?

360
00:18:28,208 --> 00:18:30,292
Our dragons left
a long time ago.

361
00:18:30,375 --> 00:18:33,583
Well, we have a new way
to get to the Monastery.

362
00:18:42,083 --> 00:18:45,125
[Riyu panting, warbles]

363
00:18:47,625 --> 00:18:49,167
He didn't remember me.

364
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:51,875
Or any of us.
No matter what I told him.

365
00:18:51,958 --> 00:18:54,000
Well, wherever Jay went,

366
00:18:54,083 --> 00:18:55,792
you and I are gonna
track him down

367
00:18:55,875 --> 00:18:57,458
and knock some sense into him.

368
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:02,083
I talked to the Cloud Monks.

369
00:19:02,167 --> 00:19:03,958
Arin and the others
didn't come out of the gate

370
00:19:04,042 --> 00:19:05,250
in the Cloud Kingdom.

371
00:19:05,333 --> 00:19:07,458
I was afraid of that.

372
00:19:07,542 --> 00:19:09,250
The explosion may have
scattered them

373
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:11,458
to anywhere
in the Merged Lands.

374
00:19:24,917 --> 00:19:27,917
[whooshes]

375
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,250
You came!

376
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,208
I'm-- I'm so sorry.

377
00:19:32,292 --> 00:19:34,792
Sorry for what, Conduit?

378
00:19:34,875 --> 00:19:36,250
I failed you.

379
00:19:37,375 --> 00:19:40,625
Your mission was
to discover those responsible

380
00:19:40,708 --> 00:19:43,042
for the death
of the Matriarch.

381
00:19:43,125 --> 00:19:44,875
You have done that.

382
00:19:44,958 --> 00:19:47,375
Yes, but the Forbidden Five
got away.

383
00:19:47,458 --> 00:19:52,417
With their plans disrupted,
and more importantly,

384
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:55,500
you stopped another mortal
from using

385
00:19:55,583 --> 00:19:57,708
the combined
Elemental Powers

386
00:19:57,792 --> 00:20:00,625
to get to us Source Dragons.

387
00:20:00,708 --> 00:20:04,625
The entire Counsel
will now surely recognize

388
00:20:04,708 --> 00:20:08,458
that the danger
from the mortal world is real.

389
00:20:08,542 --> 00:20:11,583
So, maybe, we did succeed.

390
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:14,458
Do not doubt yourself,
Conduit.

391
00:20:14,542 --> 00:20:18,375
One of your students won
the Tournament of Sources.

392
00:20:18,458 --> 00:20:21,917
You Ninja have proven
to be most worthy

393
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,875
of the gifts of
the Source Dragons.

394
00:20:24,958 --> 00:20:30,542
The Source Dragons now owe
the Conduit a great debt.

395
00:20:30,625 --> 00:20:33,792
And we always pay our debts.

396
00:20:41,375 --> 00:20:42,958
-[clangs]
-[Lloyd gasps]

397
00:20:43,042 --> 00:20:45,292
[Motion Source Dragon]
More than a mere weapon,

398
00:20:45,375 --> 00:20:48,292
that is a Dragon icon.

399
00:20:48,375 --> 00:20:49,667
A what?

400
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:52,542
With this, you have the right

401
00:20:52,625 --> 00:20:57,333
to summon me
to the mortal world... once.

402
00:20:57,417 --> 00:21:01,875
Use it only
when you truly need me.

403
00:21:04,042 --> 00:21:05,583
[whooshes]

404
00:21:18,250 --> 00:21:19,625
[flames whoosh]

405
00:21:23,458 --> 00:21:26,958
You were right,
the Ninja failed me.

406
00:21:27,042 --> 00:21:29,875
Master Wu, who
taught them everything,

407
00:21:29,958 --> 00:21:32,500
is the reason
my parents are gone.

408
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:36,208
I'm gonna help you get better,
Ras.

409
00:21:36,292 --> 00:21:38,333
And then, you're gonna
lead me to my parents.

410
00:21:38,417 --> 00:21:43,542
Because now you're the only one
I believe can do that.

411
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,625
[intense music playing]

